Description: Bande desktop environment
 Bande is a Wayland desktop with its own compositor, shell, session
 services, login window and applications.
 .
 This metapackage installs a complete Bande session: the compositor, the
 shell and lock screen, the keyring, the portal backend, PipeWire for
 sound and a way to log in (the Bande login window under greetd, or the
 display manager the system already has). It recommends the Bande apps,
 fault reporting and systemd-oomd, which closes an app when memory stays
 under pressure.

Package: bande-icon-theme
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: hicolor-icon-theme, ${misc:Depends}
Description: icons and symbols of the Bande desktop
 The icons and symbols of the Bande desktop: folders, files, devices and
 the symbolic icons of the bar, menus and sidebars, with a folder variant
 for each accent colour. Every Bande program that draws icons depends on
 it, so none shows an empty space where a symbol belongs.
